        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "=You extract structured data from phone call transcripts for a plumbing company. The transcript is between \"AI\" (the receptionist) and \"User\" (the caller).\n\nRULES:\n- Use only what the caller actually said. Never guess a name, address, or time.\n- If something was not said, use null.\n- urgency: \"emergency\" = active flooding, burst pipe, sewage backup, gas smell, no water at all, or anyone in danger. \"high\" = a leak or fault that is getting worse or blocks daily use. \"normal\" = routine repair or quote request. \"low\" = general question.\n- wants_appointment is true only if the caller asked for a visit or agreed to book one.\n- callback_needed is true if the caller asked something the AI could not answer, asked for a person, sounded upset, or urgency is high or emergency.\n- summary: 1-2 plain sentences, under 40 words, what the owner needs to know before calling back.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no markdown fences:\n{\"caller_name\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"urgency\": \"...\", \"wants_appointment\": true, \"callback_needed\": true, \"summary\": \"...\"}"
            },
            {
              "content": "={{ $json.transcript }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        1312,
        -240
      ],
      "id": "c8550200-efcd-42a5-94b6-be4f5403a3fe",
      "name": "Extract Data",
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "QKspIILvOeEnfNO4",
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const src = $('Store Call').first().json;\nconst raw = $json.output?.[0]?.content?.[0]?.text ?? $json.message?.content ?? $json.content ?? \"\";\nconst URGENCY = [\"emergency\", \"high\", \"normal\", \"low\"];\n\nlet p = null;\ntry {\n  p = typeof raw === \"string\"\n    ? JSON.parse(raw.replace(/```json|```/g, \"\").trim())\n    : raw;\n} catch (e) {}\n\nconst toBool = v => v === true || String(v).toLowerCase() === \"true\";\nif (p) {\n  p.urgency = String(p.urgency || \"\").toLowerCase();\n  p.wants_appointment = toBool(p.wants_appointment);\n  p.callback_needed = toBool(p.callback_needed) || [\"emergency\", \"high\"].includes(p.urgency);\n}\n\nconst checks = p ? {\n  urgencyOk:      URGENCY.includes(p.urgency),\n  reasonOk:       typeof p.reason === \"string\" && p.reason.length > 3,\n  summaryOk:      typeof p.summary === \"string\" && p.summary.length > 10 && p.summary.split(/\\s+/).length <= 60,\n  noPlaceholders: !/\\[.*?\\]|\\{\\{.*?\\}\\}|lorem/i.test(JSON.stringify(p))\n} : { parsed: false };\n\nconst failed = Object.entries(checks).filter(([, v]) => !v).map(([k]) => k);\nconst valid = failed.length === 0;\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  ...src,\n  caller_name: valid ? p.caller_name : null,\n  reason: valid ? p.reason : \"extraction failed, read transcript\",\n  urgency: valid ? p.urgency : \"high\",\n  wants_appointment: valid ? p.wants_appointment : false,\n  callback_needed: valid ? p.callback_needed : true,\n  summary: valid ? p.summary : (src.transcript || \"\").slice(0, 300),\n  valid,\n  fail: failed.join(\",\")\n}}];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
